# .developer-dashboard/ is excluded machine-wide by ~/.gitignore (a bare
# ".developer-dashboard" line, matching at any depth) - not by anything in
# this repo. A directory excluded that way cannot be re-included by any
# negation pattern here, in this file or any other project's: git will not
# even recurse into an excluded directory to look for one. TKT-1073, 2026-
# 09-21: the tools moved to .developer-dashboard/skills/*/cli/* and
# .developer-dashboard/cli/hooks/* are real, load-bearing tira source
# (gate-run, the push/commit-msg hooks, etc), confirmed with Michael
# (Q-178) that they must be tracked - they are added with `git add -f`,
# which bypasses ignore matching entirely rather than trying to out-rule
# the global exclude from here.
